;; YOLM FORK: Turin AVX-512 (Zen 5) lowering rules.
;;
;; This file contains ISLE lowering patterns for AVX-512 instructions
;; optimized for AMD EPYC Turin (Zen 5) processors.

;; For now, we use the existing instruction infrastructure.
;; Turin-specific optimizations will be enabled via feature flags.

;; Note: The TurinAvx512Alu MInst variant is defined in inst.isle.
;; The actual emission logic is in inst/turin/emit.rs.

;; We don't define any lowering rules here yet because:
;; 1. The $I32X16 type (512-bit vectors) isn't natively supported in Cranelift IR
;; 2. We'll need to expose these instructions through intrinsics or custom IR extensions
;;
;; When ready to lower, the pattern would be:
;; (rule N (lower (has_type ty (iadd x y)))
;;       (if-let true (use_avx512_for_type ty))
;;       (turin_vpaddd ty x y))
